            <ArticleTitle>Porcelain appendix. A calcified mucocele fractures to produce an acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>736-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mucocele of the appendix is rare and occasionally is accompanied by calcification. In a recent case, an eggshell-thin calcified mucocele fractured to produce an acute abdomen. This situation was not found in a review of the literature. A brief summary of the properties of mucocele is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
